(*
HIRR PV COHERENCE -- REFERENCE CANDIDATE, NOT A NEW TRANSACTION MODEL

Status: commentary-only audit. No trigger/call/yield annotation is introduced.
All executable declarations, guards, updates, init constraints and eight unsafe
predicates below are unchanged from examples/challenges/hirr_pvcoherence.cub.
The full 81-transition model is retained, including existing incomplete-looking
branches; this is not a repaired, reduced, or abstract-data protocol.

Claim boundary: no defensible multi-transition grouping was established in this
bounded audit. This is not a theorem that HIRR cannot be reduced. Existing local
handlers already perform their branch updates atomically. Splitting those updates
and regrouping them would create artificial novelty, not identify new isolation.

Source map (line numbers refer to the original, not this commented copy):
  6-96 types/state; 104-129 init; 138-163 eight bad-state predicates;
  168-234 stores/request/eviction issue; 236-392 owner forwarding;
  394-445 invalidation reception; 447-602 data/upgrade/put reply reception;
  606-884 L2 memory/request/upgrade handling; 885-944 writeback reception;
  946-989 unblock; 991-1036 memory reply/ack collection; 1047-1069 memory.

The process domain is parameterized. Full-data values are also proc identifiers,
with Sort=Data guards for store values and Sort=Proc for cache participants.
Sort is not initialized here; do not silently add a partition or a fixed number
of cache/data identifiers. BRAB 4 supplies a finite candidate-rejection model,
not a proof restricted to four caches or four data values. Init leaves many data
and pointer cells unconstrained, while CurrData=PrevData=MemData and caches are I.

Representation contrast: hirr_pvcoherence_abstrdata.cub removes Sort guards,
changes data-bearing cells to uninterpreted data, and writes through TempData
with nondeterministic refresh. Its store_in_e still has an unused d process
parameter. It is NOT an identical executable model or an independent protocol.
The shared 81/8 declaration counts do not prove an abstraction/refinement theorem.

Why not accepted-request -> UNBLOCK as one exclusive transaction?
  Dir_State transient values exclude many further directory requests, but not
  all ordinary actions. L1 issue/store guards do not consult Dir_State. Forwarded
  handlers deliberately accept E/M/O and MI/OI/OM_A, and invalidation handlers
  distinguish IS from IS_I and SM_A from IM_AD. Those are interference cases,
  not evidence for suppressing them. Message slots alone are not a global lock.
  transaction.ml:47-57,132-155 separates entries/exits and checks safety at
  neutral. Calling only selected successors removes other interleavings; merely
  naming a flow does not retain stores, evictions or unrelated requests inside it.
  A matching SAFE result after restriction would not validate this reduction.

Concrete source-level interference obligation (not an executed trace):
  From init, let cache a issue GETS; L2_handle_GETS_in_I, memory GETS,
  L2_Handle_data_reply_from_Memory_in_IS, exclusive reply at a, and matching
  EXCLUSIVE_UNBLOCK give a:E and Dir_State:MT. Let b issue GETS and let L2
  accept via L2_Handle_GETS_in_MT. Now Dir_State=MT_OB and a is still E.
  store_in_e(a,d) is enabled before a handles FWD_GETS and changes L1_Data[a]
  and CurrData. Eviction issue at a is also enabled and changes E to MI, selecting
  the distinct forwarded-MI branch. Guards thus do not provide whole-flow
  exclusion. This does NOT prove nonserializability: moving the store before
  acceptance may commute, but the required mover/refinement argument is absent.

Exact next investigation, NOT performed by the bounded check below:
  1. Take accepted GETS-in-MT through owner reply, recipient reply and matching
     UNBLOCK as a candidate, retaining owner a and requester b. Enumerate every
     competing transition/binding; read/write disjointness is only a first filter.
  2. For each reachable internal phase, test guard preservation and the diamond
     for moving the competitor left/right across each flow step. Compare all data,
     messages, permission and directory fields; include every intermediate bad
     predicate, not just committed endpoints. Use the original init/Sort choices.
  3. Independently enumerate the ordinary and proposed encodings for a bounded
     domain of three cache identifiers plus two Data identifiers; retain traces
     with stores before forwarding, MI/OI eviction branches, concurrent requests,
     and reply/invalidation order changes. Equality there is evidence only;
     quantify the mover/isolation proof for arbitrary finite domains separately.
  4. Resolve completion and competing ack branches literally before adding any
     recursive ack loop. For a justified proposal, mutate owner reply data to a
     stale value and require an unsafe COMPLETED-flow witness; ensure transient
     faults are not hidden by moving all eight properties to boundaries.
No mutant is delivered now: executable behavior is unchanged and no annotation
has been justified, so a mutant would not validate a new transaction model.

Experiment presentation:
  One real check was launched against this commentary-only reference with:
    /Users/kes/cubicle/cubicle.opt -nocolor -j 0 -tx none -brab 4
      -search bfsh -candheur 2 -forward-depth 31
      /Users/kes/.hermes/profiles/tetra/cache/scratch/txmodels-hirr/hirr-pvcoherence-reference.cub
  CWD: /Users/kes/.hermes/profiles/tetra/cache/scratch/txmodels-hirr/
  Observed outcome: TIMEOUT at the external 100-second bound. The process group
  was killed with SIGKILL; raw subprocess status -9; elapsed including shutdown
